# Docker deployment

From the repository root:

```sh
export REAPER_ADMIN_TOKEN='replace-me'
export REAPER_EVALUATION_TOKEN='replace-me-too'
docker compose -f deploy/docker/compose.yaml up --build
```

The Compose profile is intended for local development or a single controlled
host. Replace the example PostgreSQL password before using it outside local
development.
{{if eq .Recipe.Database.Authority "mongodb"}}
The MongoDB service runs as a single-node replica set (`--replSet rs0`); its
healthcheck initiates the replica set on first boot. The replica set is
required, not optional: the service publishes a flag definition and its audit
entry in one multi-document transaction, and MongoDB only supports
transactions on a replica set. The local profile runs without authentication;
enable access control and credentials before using it outside local
development.
{{end}}
